
This backend is built using FastAPI and serves as the core engine for the NER‑SmartRoute prototype. It connects the cleaned datasets, the trained ML risk prediction model, and the GIS route optimization logic into a single API service. The backend provides endpoints for risk prediction, route recommendation, road accessibility checks, incident reporting, alerts, and vehicle tracking. To run it, install the required Python packages (`fastapi`, `uvicorn`, `pandas`, `networkx`, `scikit‑learn`, `joblib`), then start the server with `python -m uvicorn main:app --reload`. Once running, you can test all endpoints through the interactive Swagger UI at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs`. This backend is the integration point for both the frontend website (Member 1) and the mobile app (Member 5), ensuring they can access real‑time risk, route, and logistics data.
